<title>ITALY: SWIMMING-WORLD CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-WORLD CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>IMPERIA, Italy 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results on the</p>
<p>second day of a World Cup short-course swimming meeting on</p>
<p>Wednesday:</p>
<p>Men's 50 metres freestyle</p>
<p>1. Mark Foster (Britain) 22.14 seconds</p>
<p>2. Jiang Chengji (China) 22.35</p>
<p>3. Rene Gusperti (Italy) 22.42</p>
<p>Men's 200 metres freestyle</p>
<p>1. Massimiliano Rosolino (Italy) one minute 46.66 seconds</p>
<p>2. Dimitrios Maganas (Greece) 1:48.70</p>
<p>3. Maxim Korshunov (Russia) 1:49.05</p>
<p>Men's 800 metres freestyle</p>
<p>1. Emiliano Brembilla (Italy) 7:47.64</p>
<p>2. Alexei Butsenin (Russia) 7:52.37</p>
<p>3. Alexei Akatiev (Russia) 7:54.68</p>
<p>Men's 50 metres backstroke</p>
<p>1. Tomlslav Karlo (Croatia) 24.67</p>
<p>2. Martin Harris (Britain) 25.27</p>
<p>3. Vladimir Selkov (Russia) 25.38</p>
<p>Men's 200 metres backstroke</p>
<p>1. Wang Wei (China) 1:55.65</p>
<p>2. Vladimir Selkov (Russia) 1:55.81</p>
<p>3. Emanuele Merisi (Italy) 1:55.95</p>
<p>Men's 100 metres breaststroke</p>
<p>1. Stanislav Lopukhov (Russia) 59.64</p>
<p>2. Jens Kruppa (Germany) 1:00.12</p>
<p>3. Andrei Korneev (Russia) 1:00.35</p>
</text>
